.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
.Dd October 12, 2026
.Dt LIBNAMESPACECMP 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm libnamespacecmp
.Nd system.Namespace client: jail (namespace) confinement through the BSDNamespace provider
.Sh LIBRARY
.Pq libnamespacecmp, Fl lnamespacecmp
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In namespacecmp.h
.Ft int
.Fn service_enter_namespace "struct service_context *context" "const char *path" "const char *hostname" "const char *ip4_addr" "unsigned flags"
.Ft int
.Fn service_enter_namespace_ex "struct service_context *context" "const char *path" "const char *hostname" "const char *ip4_addr" "const char *ip6_addr" "unsigned flags"
.Ft int
.Fn service_destroy_namespace "struct service_context *context"
.Ft int
.Fn service_namespace_info "struct service_context *context" "struct service_namespace_info *out"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These calls were part of
.Xr libservice 3
and moved to their own library with the same names and semantics.
Each takes the process's own service context from
.Xr service_acquire 3 ;
a context inherited across a fork is refused with
.Er EINVAL .
The calls speak the FIDL library
.Li bsd.namespace.v1
.Pq Pa /usr/share/fidl/namespacecmp.fidl
to the provider.
The process-wide session is opened by name on first use and negotiated
once; a forked child abandons the parent's session and opens its own.
Each call is bounded by 30 seconds, shortened by an active
.Xr service_budget_begin 3 .
A timeout, a transport failure or a malformed reply drops the session, and
the next call opens a new one; an application error keeps it.
.Pp
.Fn service_enter_namespace
asks the
.Dq system.Namespace
provider
.Pq Xr BSDNamespace 8
to create a jail rooted at
.Fa path
(scoped by this process's channel label) and attaches the calling process to it;
the returned jail's root credential authorizes the attach, so a non-root caller
may confine itself.
.Fa hostname
and
.Fa ip4_addr
may be
.Dv NULL .
.Fa flags
is zero for a persistent jail (reused by label across restarts) or
.Dv SERVICE_NS_EPHEMERAL
for a jail whose lifetime is bound to the calling process.
.Pp
.Fn service_enter_namespace_ex
is
.Fn service_enter_namespace
with an additional IPv6 address
.Fa ip6_addr
.Pq empty or Dv NULL for none
and the full
.Dv SERVICE_NS_*
flag set, including
.Dv SERVICE_NS_VNET
for a jail with its own virtual network stack (requires
.Dv VIMAGE ) .
.Fn service_enter_namespace
is this with
.Fa ip6_addr
empty.
.Pp
.Fn service_destroy_namespace
destroys the caller's own jail, scoped to the caller's label so it can never
name another's;
.Er ENOENT
is returned when the caller has none.
.Pp
.Fn service_namespace_info
reports the caller's own jail into
.Fa out .
A label owns at most one jail:
.Va out->present
is 1 with the fields filled, or 0 when the caller has no jail (which is still a
success).
.Va out->flags
carries the
.Dv SERVICE_NS_*
bits describing the jail \(em
.Dv SERVICE_NS_VNET
when it has its own virtual network stack, and
.Dv SERVICE_NS_EPHEMERAL
when this process's own connection is anchoring the jail's lifetime \(em so a
consumer that lists after a restart can pass them straight back to
.Fn service_enter_namespace_ex .
Each address field is empty when the jail has no address of that family.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Rv -std service_enter_namespace service_enter_namespace_ex service_destroy_namespace service_namespace_info
.Sh ERRORS
In addition to the provider's
.Xr errno 2
values (for example
.Er EEXIST , EALREADY , ENOENT
or the jail gate's errors):
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Bq Er EINVAL
An argument was invalid, or
.Fa context
is not this process's own service context.
.It Bq Er EPROTO
The provider's reply was malformed; any descriptor it carried was closed.
.It Bq Er EPROTONOSUPPORT
The provider speaks a different wire version.
.It Bq Er ETIMEDOUT
The provider did not answer in time.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr libservice 3 ,
.Xr BSDNamespace 8
.Sh HISTORY
These functions appeared in
.Xr libservice 3 ;
.Nm libnamespacecmp
appeared in 5BSD when they moved out of it, and its record protocol was
replaced by
.Li bsd.namespace.v1
in October 2026.
